{
 "$description": "Snapshot of the LIVE SAMAVESH Figma library — fileKey 3FF5l0SMNIwdpZrKkeyPTm, the canonical one named in GOVERNANCE.md. TWO OLDER COPIES still exist and still contain variables (qyzTEy8… 261 vars, T3bkN5g… 176), so a sync run against either looks successful and reaches nobody: check the count before writing. Variable names ARE the canonical DTCG paths, so this file doubles as the proof that the Figma tree and the source tree are the same tree.",
 "$readAt": "2026-08-10",
 "$note": "2026-08-10, SIXTH pass — the six gaps the audit named. icon/size/* (5, the estate default is md=24px and was hardcoded per component), focus/width + focus/offset (the ring's COLOUR was tokenised long before its geometry, leaving WCAG 2.4.7's most-regulated affordance two-thirds hardcoded), container/* (5, incl. the 1280px content width mandated in CLAUDE.md that existed only as a literal), elevation/* (6 semantic levels over the raw shadow ramp — CSS only, since Figma models shadows as EFFECT STYLES not variables), motion/{enter,exit,emphasis} (a duration paired with the easing that belongs to it — a bare duration loses the pairing), and control/{radius,border/width}. Routing had to become TYPE-AWARE: focus, icon and control each own both a colour and a measurement, so routing by root alone put five FLOATs in the colour collection.",
